      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4j7",
          "text": "A ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4j8",
          "text": "ski knee injury",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4j9",
          "text": " can turn a perfect day on the slopes into months of pain, rehabilitation, and uncertainty. In Vail or other Colorado ski towns, where the terrain challenges even seasoned skiers, knee injuries happen more often than many realize. The impact goes beyond the knee from sudden twists that strain ligaments to ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jb",
          "text": "collisions that leave lasting damage",
          "marks": [
            "l4ja"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jc",
          "text": "—it can disrupt work, finances, and family life. Taking the right steps can make a significant difference in both recovery and your legal options. At ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4je",
          "text": "Dormer Harpring",
          "marks": [
            "l4jd",
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jf",
          "text": ", when insurance companies and negligent parties threaten your future, we fight to protect your health, your rights, and your recovery.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "image",
      "_key": "i4jh",
      "src": "./images/2025-12-shutterstock_542540116-1-300x200.jpg",
      "alt": "Ski Knee Injury"
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4jj",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4ji",
          "text": "Common Knee Injuries in Skiing in Vail, Colorado",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4jl",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jk",
          "text": "Skiing demands agility, balance, and constant adaptation to unpredictable conditions. When things go wrong, the knee is often the first joint to absorb the impact. Some of the most frequent injuries we see in ski cases include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4jo",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jm",
          "text": "Anterior Cruciate Ligament (ACL) Tears",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jn",
          "text": " occur when the ligament that stabilizes the knee joint ruptures. They often require surgery and extensive rehabilitation.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4jr",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jp",
          "text": "Medial Collateral Ligament (MCL) Sprains",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jq",
          "text": ": Caused by sudden twisting or side pressure, these sprains can range from mild stretching to severe tears.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4ju",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4js",
          "text": "Meniscus Tears",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jt",
          "text": ": The cartilage cushions the joint can tear during sharp turns or sudden stops.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4jx",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jv",
          "text": "Fractures and Dislocations",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jw",
          "text": ": Though less common, they carry long-term complications and may involve surgical correction.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4jz",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4jy",
          "text": "These injuries not only impact your ability to return to skiing; they also affect mobility in everyday life. We’ve seen clients facing months of physical therapy and significant financial stress.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4k1",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4k0",
          "text": "How to Prevent Knee Injuries While Skiing",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4k3",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4k2",
          "text": "Prevention starts before you step onto the lift. Proper preparation and awareness can reduce your chances of suffering a debilitating knee injury. Key prevention strategies include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4k6",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4k4",
          "text": "Conditioning before ski season",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4k5",
          "text": ": Strength training, balance exercises, and flexibility routines prepare muscles and ligaments for the demands of skiing.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4k9",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4k7",
          "text": "Using well-fitted gear",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4k8",
          "text": ": Ill-fitted boots or bindings increase the risk of injury. Have a professional adjust your equipment each season.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4kc",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4ka",
          "text": "Learning safe techniques",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kb",
          "text": ": Take a refresher lesson to practice proper stance, controlled turns, and fall techniques.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4kf",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kd",
          "text": "Warming up",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4ke",
          "text": ": Cold muscles are more prone to strain. Simple stretches and light aerobic activity before hitting the slopes can make a difference.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4kk",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l4kh",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.cumedicine.us/health-insights/ski-injuries-treatment-prevention-and-getting-back-on-the-slopes?utm_source=chatgpt.com"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kg",
          "text": "The ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4ki",
          "text": "University of Colorado School of Medicine",
          "marks": [
            "l4kh"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kj",
          "text": " outlines that preparation and technique are essential to lowering ski-related knee injury rates.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4km",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kl",
          "text": "What to Do If You Hurt Your Knee While Skiing in Vail, Colorado",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4ko",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kn",
          "text": "Even the most skilled and cautious skier can experience an accident on the mountain. Vail is world-renowned for its challenging terrain, diverse runs, and heavy ski traffic, but those features also increase the likelihood of collisions and falls. When a ski knee injury happens, the actions you take in the minutes, hours, and days afterward will shape your recovery and your legal options if negligence is involved. Below is a detailed, step-by-step guide to follow.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4kq",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kp",
          "text": "Stop Skiing",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4ks",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kr",
          "text": "The first and most crucial step is to stop immediately. Many skiers try to “push through” a knee injury, hoping it’s a minor tweak that will ease up with time. This is one of the worst things you can do. Skiing on an unstable or injured joint can cause further tearing of ligaments, worsen swelling, and even create permanent damage that requires surgery. Resort safety patrol is trained to assist; flag them down or have a fellow skier call for help. Continuing down the slope alone risks additional falls and greater injury.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4ku",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kt",
          "text": "Assess the Injury",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4kw",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kv",
          "text": "Once you are in a safe location, take a moment to evaluate what happened. Ask yourself:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4ky",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kx",
          "text": "Can you move your leg in all directions?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4l0",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4kz",
          "text": "Is it possible to bear weight without sharp pain?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4l2",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4l1",
          "text": "Does the knee feel unstable, as if it might “give out”?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4l4",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4l3",
          "text": "Did you hear or feel a “popping” sound at the moment of injury?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4l6",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4l5",
          "text": "Rapid swelling is another warning sign that something more serious than a bruise or minor strain has occurred. If you are unable to stand or if pain intensifies quickly, seek medical help immediately.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4l8",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4l7",
          "text": "Apply RICE",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4la",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4l9",
          "text": "RICE—Rest, Ice, Compression, Elevation—remains the gold standard for immediate injury care. Here’s how to apply it effectively on the mountain and afterward:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4ld",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lb",
          "text": "Rest",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lc",
          "text": ": Stop all activity that places weight on the injured leg. Accept help from ski patrol to reach medical facilities or safe transport.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4lg",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4le",
          "text": "Ice",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lf",
          "text": ": Apply a cold pack or snow wrapped in cloth for 15–20 minutes. Never apply ice directly to bare skin, as it can cause frostbite.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4lj",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lh",
          "text": "Compression",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4li",
          "text": ": Use an elastic bandage to stabilize the joint and control swelling until a professional can examine it.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4lm",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lk",
          "text": "Elevation",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4ll",
          "text": ": Raise the leg above heart level when possible, even if only while sitting and waiting for transport.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4lo",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4ln",
          "text": "RICE will not cure a ligament or cartilage injury, but can minimize swelling and pain until definitive treatment begins.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4lq",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lp",
          "text": "Seek Medical Attention",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4ls",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lr",
          "text": "Prompt medical evaluation does more than confirm the extent of the injury. It creates a written medical record that documents the injury’s severity, timing, and likely cause. These records are critical if questions of liability arise—whether another skier’s reckless behavior caused the crash or a resort failed to mark dangerous terrain. Keep copies of all bills, reports, and treatment plans. They guide recovery and establish proof of damages in a legal claim.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4lu",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lt",
          "text": "Rehabilitation",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4lw",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lv",
          "text": "Rehabilitation is often the most extended and most demanding part of recovery from a ski knee injury. Treatment may range from several weeks of physical therapy for mild sprains to reconstructive surgery followed by a year of rehabilitation for major ligament tears. Documenting this process is important for both recovery and any potential claim.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4ly",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lx",
          "text": "Be Aware of Your Rights",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4m6",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l4m0",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://law.justia.com/codes/colorado/title-33/recreational-areas-and-ski-safety/article-44/"
        },
        {
          "_key": "l4m3",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb21-184"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4lz",
          "text": "Colorado law acknowledges that skiing carries “inherent dangers and risks,” including terrain changes, weather conditions, and collisions with natural objects. Under the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4m1",
          "text": "Colorado Ski Safety and Liability Act (C.R.S. § 33-44)",
          "marks": [
            "l4m0",
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4m2",
          "text": ", ski area operators are generally not liable for injuries caused by these inherent risks. However, the Act clarifies that negligence, such as failing to mark hazards, operating lifts unsafely, or ignoring statutory safety duties, does not fall within that protection. In fact, amendments like ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4m4",
          "text": "Senate Bill 21-184",
          "marks": [
            "l4m3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4m5",
          "text": " strengthened specific skier responsibilities and clarified liability rules. This means that if your injury stems from another party’s negligence, you may still pursue compensation under Colorado law.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4m8",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4m7",
          "text": "Call a Ski Crash Injury Lawyer That Understands the Rules",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4mh",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l4mc",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/contact/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4m9",
          "text": "A ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4ma",
          "text": "ski knee injury",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4mb",
          "text": " can derail more than your season on the slopes—it can bring overwhelming medical expenses, weeks of lost work, and complex questions about liability. At Dormer Harpring, we take on the legal fight so you can focus on recovery. ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
